## Smoke test 1 — one-shot prompt on the default model

Attempt 1 (primary route). Command:
```
prime-agent -p --no-session "Reply with exactly: routing-ok"
```
Output (verbatim):
```
402 Insufficient balance (including overdraft). Please add funds to continue. Requests are authenticated by PRIME_API_KEY and billed to the personal balance unless the request includes X-Prime-Team-ID. Add funds to the selected balance. If you intended to use team billing, send X-Prime-Team-ID with the team ID and make sure that team has funds. See https://docs.primeintellect.ai/inference/troubleshooting#insufficient-funds.
exit=1
```

Attempt 2 (documented fallback tier, `providerBackupModel` target). Command:
```
prime-agent -p --no-session --provider zai --model glm-5.3-flash "Reply with exactly: routing-ok"
```
Output (verbatim):
```
routing-ok
exit=0
```

**Verdict: PASS ON REROUTE / FAIL ON PRIMARY** — the primary route
(openai-codex → gpt-6-sol) is quota-blocked with 402 Insufficient balance
(exact error above); the run rerouted to `zai/glm-5.3-flash` and the
reroute passed cleanly. The response path itself (auth, request, reply)
works end-to-end on the fallback tier.

