## Smoke test 2 — RLM subagent spawn (rlm.spawn → rlm.collect)

Attempt 1 (`-p` primary, per docs/smoke-testing.md). Command:
```
prime-agent -p --no-session "Spawn a subagent with rlm.spawn(prompt='Reply with exactly: subagent-ok', name='smoke-probe'). Do not pass model or thinking. Then call rlm.collect(timeout_ms=120000) and print the child's reply verbatim, plus whatever the reply/session shows about which model the child ran on."
```
Output: same verbatim `402 Insufficient balance …` error as test 1, `exit=1`.

Attempt 2 (`-p`, root rerouted to zai). Command: same prompt with
`--provider zai --model glm-5.3-flash`. Output (key lines verbatim):
```
RuntimeError: rlm.spawn requires a daemon-backed session: this session has no RLM child runtime
```
(The root model call succeeded; the spawn itself was refused by the RLM
host. `rlm.list_subagents()` → `[]`, `rlm.collect(timeout_ms=0)` → `[]`,
`agent_observe.list` likewise unavailable:
`RuntimeError: host request type "agent_observe.list" is not available in this session`.)

Attempt 3 (`-p` with explicit daemon socket of the running daemon).
Command: same prompt plus
`--daemon-socket /tmp/prime-agent-rust-1000/daemon.sock --provider zai --model glm-5.3-flash`.
Output (key lines verbatim): identical refusals —
```
RuntimeError: rlm.spawn requires a daemon-backed session: this session has no RLM child runtime
rlm.create_session requires a daemon-backed depth-0 session
```
Conclusion: `-p` sessions never get the RLM child runtime, regardless of
daemon socket — the doc's `-p` form of this test cannot pass on 0.10.0.

Attempt 4 — the doc's documented interactive equivalent ("open prime-agent,
then give the same instruction in chat"), run as a fresh headless TUI
session in a pty on the shared daemon (separate agent from the operator's;
stopped afterwards), root on zai since codex is quota-blocked. Command:
```
prime-agent --provider zai --model glm-5.3-flash 'Run two probes in order and report both verbatim.
Probe A: call rlm.spawn(prompt="Reply with exactly: subagent-ok", name="smoke-probe") with NO model and NO thinking arguments. Then call rlm.collect(timeout_ms=120000). Print the child reply verbatim, plus any info the handle/reply/session shows about which model and thinking level the child ran on.
…'
```
(session `01a12cb2-9908-766c-8982-17ff003546a0`). Output (verbatim from
the session transcript):

Spawn handle:
```
rlm_child_id: sub-c0db53e3
name: smoke-probe
session_dir: /home/vgpnk/.prime/agent/session-artifacts/01a12cb2-9908-766c-8982-17ff003546a0/sub-c0db53e3
model: zai/glm-5.3-flash
```
Final collect:
```
rlm_child_id: 'sub-c0db53e3'
session_name: 'smoke-probe'
status: 'done'
settled: True
answer_preview: 'Replied to the parent with exactly: `subagent-ok`. Task complete; going idle.'
error: None
duration_ms: 64696
```
Child reply (arrived via agent_message → collect): `subagent-ok`
Child session log model events:
```
{"type":"model_change", "provider":"zai", "modelId":"glm-5.3-flash"}
{"type":"thinking_level_change", "thinkingLevel":"high"}
{"type":"service_tier_change", "serviceTier":"default"}
```
Subagent registry (`rlm-subagent.json`):
```json
{"type":"rlm_subagent","childId":"sub-c0db53e3","sessionName":"smoke-probe","prompt":"Reply with exactly: subagent-ok","model":{"provider":"zai","modelId":"glm-5.3-flash"},"status":"completed"}
```
Child log contains **zero** 402 entries and no codex attempt — the child
went straight to the inherited model.

Disambiguation probe (is the child's zai model a quota reroute of
`subagentDefaultModel`, or is the setting ignored?): identical one-shot
spawn with the parent on a different provider,
`prime-agent --provider kimi-coding --model kimi-for-coding '…rlm.spawn(prompt="Reply with exactly: subagent-ok", name="smoke-probe-2") with NO model and NO thinking arguments…'`
(session `01a12cb7-6618-7568-87f0-6873eecb53cd`). Output (verbatim):
```
subagent-ok            (child reply, via agent_message)
handle.model: kimi-coding/kimi-for-coding
status: done, settled: True, error: None, duration_ms: 65942
```
The child again inherited the parent model. `subagentDefaultModel`
(gpt-5.1-codex-mini) was not resolved in either run.

**Verdict: SPLIT —**
- Spawn mechanism (`rlm.spawn` → `agent_message` → `rlm.collect`, depth-1
  under `rlmMaxDepth: 3`): **PASS** — child spawned, replied
  `subagent-ok`, collected `done`/`settled`/`error: None`, twice.
- Expected subagent-model routing (child resolves to
  `gpt-5.1-codex-mini` when no model is passed): **FAIL** — children
  inherit the parent's model and thinking regardless of
  `subagentDefaultModel` (verified with two different parent providers;
  child logs show the setting was never consulted). The observed runs are
  therefore parent-inheritance, not a backup reroute of the codex-mini
  lane. See Findings F1.

