## Findings (outside M7 scope — filed to the tower, not fixed here)

- **F1 — `subagentDefaultModel` is not honored by spawn resolution** on
  prime-agent 0.10.0: with the key set to `gpt-5.1-codex-mini` and
  `rlm.spawn` called with no `model=`, children inherited the parent's
  provider/model/thinking in both probes (zai parent → zai child;
  kimi-coding parent → kimi-coding child); child session logs contain no
  attempt to resolve the setting. Volume-lane routing to codex-mini does
  not happen via this key on this build.
- **F2 — `-p` sessions have no daemon-backed host surface**: `rlm.spawn`,
  `rlm.create_session`, `refine.status`, `agent_observe.*` all refuse with
  "requires a daemon-backed session" / "host request type … is not
  available in this session", even with `--daemon-socket` pointed at the
  live daemon. docs/smoke-testing.md's `-p` commands for tests 2 and 3
  cannot pass as written; the interactive-session equivalents work.
- **F3 — `rlm.collect(timeout_ms=…)` does not block** to settlement as
  documented: first call returned in `duration_ms: 1` with
  `status: 'running'`; callers must re-poll (both probes settled only
  after ~65 s of polling).
- **F4 — openai-codex provider is quota-blocked** (402 Insufficient
  balance, verbatim under test 1): affects the default route (gpt-6-sol),
  the auxiliary/subagent lane (gpt-5.1-codex-mini) and every codex model
  until the personal balance is funded or team billing (X-Prime-Team-ID)
  is configured. The zai tier (`glm-5.3-flash`) passes; the kimi-coding
  tier also passed in the disambiguation probe.

